---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { SITE } from "../lib/constants";

const updated = "1 November 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="FollowExam privacy policy — what data we collect, how it is used and the rights you have over it."
  gated={false}
>
  <section class="section-tight" style="padding-top:34px">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="breadcrumb" style="padding:0 0 14px">
        <a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><span>Privacy</span>
      </div>

      <article class="prose">
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="small muted">Last updated: {updated}</p>

        <p>
          FollowExam respects your privacy. This policy explains what data we collect, why we collect it and how you
          can control it.
        </p>

        <h2>1. Data we collect</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Account data</strong> — your name, email address or phone number, and the sign-in provider you use.</li>
          <li><strong>Profile data</strong> — your state, education level, stream, date of birth, career goal, interests and alert preference.</li>
          <li><strong>Saved updates</strong> — the notifications you bookmark inside your account.</li>
          <li><strong>Technical data</strong> — browser type, device type, approximate location and page visits.</li>
          <li><strong>Messages</strong> — anything you send through the contact form or email.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>2. How we use data</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>To run your account and keep your profile available across devices.</li>
          <li>To recommend exams, institutions and scholarships that match your profile.</li>
          <li>To send the daily email digest if you turn alerts on.</li>
          <li>To improve site speed, content and usability.</li>
          <li>To prevent spam, abuse and security issues.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>3. Who we share data with</h2>
        <p>
          We do not sell your personal data. Data is shared only with the service providers needed to run the site, such
          as Firebase (Google) for authentication, database and hosting, and an email delivery service for alerts. Those
          providers handle data under their own privacy terms.
        </p>

        <h2>4. Cookies and local storage</h2>
        <p>
          The site uses cookies and local storage for your login session, saved preferences and basic analytics. You can
          block cookies in your browser settings, but some features will stop working.
        </p>

        <h2>5. Email alerts and unsubscribe</h2>
        <p>
          Every alert email includes an unsubscribe option. You can also turn alerts off from your profile at any time.
          After an unsubscribe request we do not send marketing email.
        </p>

        <h2>6. Data retention</h2>
        <p>
          Account data is kept until you delete your profile or ask us to delete it. Contact messages are kept for a
          reasonable period and then deleted.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Children's privacy</h2>
        <p>
          FollowExam does not knowingly collect personal data from children under 13. If you believe a minor's data has
          been collected, contact us and we will remove it.
        </p>

        <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Request a copy of your data.</li>
          <li>Ask for a correction.</li>
          <li>Delete your profile and saved updates from the profile page.</li>
          <li>Turn email alerts off at any time.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          For these requests write to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>9. Third-party links</h2>
        <p>
          Our posts link to official government websites. Those websites have their own privacy policies and you should
          read them. FollowExam is not responsible for their content or data practices.
        </p>

        <h2>10. Policy updates</h2>
        <p>
          This policy may change from time to time. We will post a notice on the site for major changes. The latest
          version is always on this page.
        </p>

        <h2>11. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          For any privacy question: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
